<title>GREECE: Greek Sept building materials prices up 7.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Greek Sept building materials prices up 7.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's building materials price index for new housing rose 7.1 percent year-on-year in September against a 6.9 percent increase in August and 8.6 percent in the same month in 1995, the National Statistics Service(NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The index was up an average 7.4 percent year-on-year in the period January-September, the same as in 1995, NSS said.</p>
<p>					Sept 96   Aug 96  Sept 95</p>
<p>     Month/month change(pct)    2.2%     0.1%     2.0%</p>
<p>     Year-on-year(pct)	    7.1%     6.9%     8.6%</p>
<p>     Index (1990=100)	    189.0     184.9   176.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
